// The terrain manifest: what the shipped heightmap IS, and the extent it is hung at.
//
// This file is the map's presence marker (`terrain_grid::decode_height_grid`). Absent, the world
// falls back to the flat slab + authored test course; present, everything it names must load or the
// process panics (ADR-0011) — a peer silently going flat while others load the map would desync the
// deterministic sim.
//
// `heightmap` resolves against this file's own directory. Grayscale PNG, square, any bit depth:
// the decoder normalizes to full-scale-relative values before scaling, so 8- and 16-bit sources
// interchange (16-bit is what ships — see `terrain_grid::SMOOTH_SIGMA_PX` for what 8 bits costs).
// Image axes: column -> +X, row -> -Z, pixel (0, 0) at the (-X, +Z) corner.
//
// AUTHORED values, not derived: the author states the export's vertical range and the extent the
// map is meant to cover. `height_offset_m` is the metre height a full-scale-zero sample maps to and
// `height_span_m` the metres a full-scale sample adds on top, so decoded height is
// `offset + normalized * span`.
(
    heightmap: "terrain_height.png",
    world_size_m: 1500.0,
    height_offset_m: 0.0,
    height_span_m: 50.0,
)
